WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Quebec's new separatist government has pledged an independence referendum despite winning only a minority of seats. This is Omni View, episode 197. The party Quebec was secured the most seats in Monday's provincial election but fell short of a majority in the National Assembly, which has 127 seats. The party captured nearly 60 of those seats. Leader Paul St. Pierre Plamondon said the results showed voters want the party to work with others while still advancing.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.380
fancy sovereignty. He ruled out holding a referendum while Donald Trump remains US President.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.240
The campaign platform included reducing ties to the British monarchy and preparing another

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.880
vote on leaving Canada. Federalist parties have already signaled resistance, and recent

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:54.400
polls have shown roughly 30% support for independence. The last such vote in 1995 produced a narrow

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:00.380
no. That seat count, the poll number, and the missing majority are the ground every serious

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.520
account is using. Deutschewelle treats the victory speech and the seat totals as a return

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.700
of long-dormant separatist momentum, a party that asked for a path towards sovereignty,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:17.000
and then won more seats than anyone else. AP News puts those same totals beside the minority

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.340
result and opposition reactions, and Federalist parties treat the 30% figure as proof that

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.340
another vote would not carry the province.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.340
Al Jazeera describes a renewed push for a third referendum.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.020
Canadian constitutional rules still require the province to seek federal approval or

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.500
negotiate terms for any binding vote, a step that has historically meant lengthy legal and

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.460
political wrangling.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.700
The Pentagon withdrew roughly a dozen B-1 bombers from Royal Air Force Fairford, a British

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.940
base, and returned them to U.S. stations.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.580
President Trump stated that intelligence about threats prompted the move rather than any

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.300
accident, the BBC reports.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.920
The exact nature of the threat remains unclear, though US media have linked it to possible

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.260
Iranian drone or sabotage plans.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.980
British officials had earlier described the base as secure and pointed to prior praise from

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.100
Trump for UK security services.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:19.440
BBC reporting notes Washington sources citing Ukraine's Operation Spider-Web as a model

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.560
of what distant attackers might attempt.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.100
The economic times carried Trump's on-camera remarks on the withdrawal.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:32.000
The decision comes amid heightened regional tensions, but does not alter the overall U.S. military

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.120
posture in Europe.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.040
Ukrainian forces sent approximately 650 drones toward the Moscow region overnight.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.240
Russian air defenses destroyed most at long range, yet two people were reported killed and

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.260
several injured, according to the South China Morning Post.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:54.300
First, Moscow mayor Sergei Sabianin described it as the second largest such assault in recent

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:54.720
years.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.600
France 24 recorded the scale of the strike and the resulting casualties in suburban areas.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.860
Russian authorities said the attack followed a pattern of stepped-up Ukrainian operations.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.760
Ukrainian statements framed it as retaliation within the ongoing conflict.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.920
Air defenses intercepted most of the drones far from the capital.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:21.620
The incident adds to the cycle of long-range strikes without immediate indication of a shift in battlefield lines.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:28.140
Ambassador Hillel Newman holds Guardian Australia that the third anniversary of the October 7th attacks

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.420
offers a chance to restore traditional friendship despite recent strains.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.200
He acknowledged policy differences but urged both governments not to let them dominate the relationship.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:45.320
In that telling, the anniversary is a moment to keep a long alliance from being defined by the fights of the past few years.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:51.060
Palestinian community leaders in Australia have called for more federal support for their diaspora,

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:58.060
and they want greater official recognition of their community's concerns rather than a reset that sets those concerns aside.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:06.740
Relations deteriorated after 2023 over Australian criticism of settler violence in the West Bank and other Gaza-related issues.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:11.860
news. Newman's comments come after Israel's foreign ministry publicly rebuked Australian

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.980
foreign minister Penny Wong on social media. The Guardian piece sets the ambassadors

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:23.940
outreach next to that counterview from Palestinian representatives. US Startup Reflection AI unveiled

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:30.280
Beam, an open-weight model, one whose train parameters are released for others to run, aimed

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:36.380
at coding, reasoning, and tasks in which software acts step-by-step toward a goal. Nvidia

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:43.080
India backs the company. Early tests indicate Beam uses 3-4 times less inference compute, meaning

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:48.700
the computing power needed to run it than comparable open models, while matching or approaching

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:54.720
several Chinese systems on specific benchmarks. The company positioned Beam as competitive with

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:04.000
Jipu AI is GLM 5.2 and close to Alibaba's Quinn 3.8 Max, though moonshot AI's Kimi-K3 still

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.680
leads in raw capability. South China Morning Post coverage highlights a U.S. effort to counter

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.380
Chinese dominance in freely available models and treats NVIDIA's backing as a factor in the

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:21.500
efficiency claims. Computer-driven trend following funds, programs that bet an asset's recent

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:27.500
direction will continue, posted a 15.7% return in the first nine months of the year,

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:36.320
beating the S&amp;P 500's 11.7% gain CNBC reports. The funds profited from short positions in bonds

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.920
during September's sell-off and from earlier long bets on oil ahead of regional conflict. CNBC

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:48.380
attributes the results to quantitative models that identified momentum in rates, currencies and

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:55.560
commodities while equities rose on artificial intelligence or AI enthusiasm. Industry participants

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.140
Americans noted that machines avoided emotional timing errors that affected

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.140
discrepanary investors. Systematic strategies can exploit

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:07.660
divergences between asset classes when traditional 60-40 portfolios face

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:12.140
pressure. A new state media documentary is a record of what's actually

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.760
being done against cross-border scam compounds.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.720
And it documents three Chinese attempts to shut those operations down in Myanmar.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:24.320
The three-part series produced jointly by China's Ministry of Public

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:30.480
security and the state broadcaster CCTV, details three rounds of efforts to persuade powerful

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.340
families in northern Myanmar to close the compounds. Those approaches came before Myanmar police

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:43.160
conducted a major arrest operation in 2023. The films describe obstacles faced in cross-border

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.880
enforcement. South China Morning Post coverage notes the documentary's focus on the scale of the

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.760
criminal networks and the diplomatic steps taken prior to the arrests.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:58.180
The account is a record of repeated official engagement rather than a single intervention,

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:03.320
and the operation's persistence until the police action shows the limits of that engagement.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.560
To really understand how a minority government pursues a sovereignty referendum in Canada, look

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.540
at the assembly's voting rules, not the victory speech.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:18.140
A common reading treats a separatist election win as an automatic path to a ballot on leaving

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:24.040
the country. Canada's parliamentary rules work differently. The winning party still has to secure

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:30.120
support from other legislators for major constitutional steps. In practice, a minority government

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:35.700
must negotiate confidence and supply agreements, deals in which smaller parties keep a government

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:41.740
in office, and vote for its budgets without joining a full coalition. Or it can lose power before

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:47.720
any referendum bill even passes the provincial assembly. Historical precedent goes further than that

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:53.740
minority math. Even majority separatist governments needed federal cooperation and court rulings

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:59.540
to define the terms of a vote after the last province-wide independence ballot. Knowing the mechanism,

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:04.940
you can treat a mandate for independence headline as a claim to test rather than a result that has

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:10.560
already happened. The test is whether the governing party has actually secured cross-party backing

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:16.660
for legislation, not whether it finished first on election night. Official seat counts from elections

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.980
Quebec, read against party platforms and the assembly's own records, show what a minority

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:27.600
can pass without extra votes. One concrete check in the first legislative session is simple,

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.160
a formal referendum bill on the order paper, and a second party willing to vote for it.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.380
Deutschewella is building the Quebec result around seat totals and the victory speech,

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:44.160
while AP news is building it around the minority arithmetic and how opponents have already answered.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:49.720
The third anniversary of the October 7th attacks will arrive as a public moment in Australia

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.020
Israel relations, with both governments already on the record about whether policy fights

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.880
should define the whole relationship.

